# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env files: .env.local and friends hold real values for local runs
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Secrets & credentials — none are committed today; these patterns are
# belt-and-suspenders so a stray key can't slip into a public repo. The
# wildcards on both sides are deliberate: the filenames that actually
# occur are prefixed, not bare (ADC writes
# application_default_credentials.json, and google-github-actions/auth
# drops gha-creds-*.json into the workspace).
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
*-creds-*.json
key*.json
sa-*.json

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Playwright MCP verification artifacts (docs/testing.md)
.playwright-mcp/

# OpenTofu (deploy/opentofu): state stays in GCS after bootstrap, and
# tfvars carry account-specific values (billing account, suffix) that
# don't belong in a public repo. Lock files ARE committed.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
tfplan
*.tfplan

# Test output. e2e/.gitignore covers the same names one level down; these
# catch a run started from the repo root.
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Scratchpad file
~notes.txt
